<worksheet >
    <title>IC-2 Triple Integrals</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete both problems. 
      To earn a P on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete Problem 1 and 
      one part of Problem 2</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="2.5in">
      <p>Evaluate <m>\iiint_E y dV</m> where 
        <m>E=\left\{(x,y,z)|0\le z\le1, 0\le x\le z, 0\le y\le x+z\right\}</m></p></exercise>
  </page>
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
      <task><statement><p>Let <m>\iiint_D y dV</m> be such that <m>D</m> is 
        the solid region inside the cylinder <m>x^2+y^2=9</m>, above the plane 
        <m>z=0</m>, and below the plane <m>z=x+4</m>. Use cylindrical coordinates 
        to set up the integration that will give the volume.</p>
    </statement></task>
      <task><statement><p>Let <m>\iiint_D (x^2+y^2+z^2) dV</m> be such that 
        <m>D</m> is the solid region bounded by the sphere <m>\rho=2</m> and 
        the cones <m>\phi=\frac{\pi}{6}</m> and <m>\phi=\frac{\pi}{3}</m>. Use 
        spherical coordinates to set up the integration that will give the volume.</p>
    </statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>